Attach a bust portrait to a character (no generation, free).

A portrait is the starting frame for talking animations — set one, then
create_vocal_animation generates the mouth positions from it. Overwrites any
existing portrait.

Examples:
- Straight from a portrait job:
  set_character_portrait("<character-uuid>", from_job_id="<portrait-job-uuid>")
- From your own artwork:
  set_character_portrait("<character-uuid>", image=<png_base64>)

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__pixellab__set_character_portrait(args: {
  // Character to attach the portrait to.
  character_id: string;
  // Instead of `image`: the job id of a completed create_portrait_character run. The sprite is copied straight across, so it never has to pass through your context.
  from_job_id?: string | null;
  // Portrait as base64-encoded PNG. Square is ideal; a non-square image is centred on a transparent square canvas.
  image?: string | null;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__pixellab__unzoom_image","description":"PixelLab AI-powered pixel art generation service.

